        "text": "Page: Champlain Canal. Sentence: The Champlain Canal is a 60 mi canal that connects the south end of Lake Champlain to the Hudson River in New York.\nPage: Warren County Canal. Sentence: The Warren County Canal was a branch of the Miami and Erie Canal in southwestern Ohio about 20 mi in length that connected the Warren County seat of Lebanon to the main canal at Middletown in the mid-19th century.\nPage: Glens Falls Feeder Canal. Sentence: It is 7 mi long and delivers water from above Glen's Falls on the Hudson River to the highest point of the Champlain Canal.",
